\f0\fs24 \cf2 Sometimes it truly feels as if time has stood still. Looking at the Fresco Room, it\'92s hard to believe that more than a hundred years have passed: the arrangement has remained almost exactly as it was when the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers lived here.\
Everything is still in its place, even the 16th-century candlesticks are exactly where they left them.\
And above the 
\f1\i Cassone delle Virt\'f9
\f0\i0 ? The objects that once adorned it are still the same, though today they\'92re kept inside a display case to protect them, but also to let us admire them up close.\
But not everything has remained frozen: there\'92s one detail that has changed its place.\
Next to the fresco, there once was a bas-relief... which today can be found in another room of the museum.\
A small mystery to solve: will you be able to find it?\
